# API base URL. Leave unset in development — Vite proxies /api to the backend
# (see vite.config.ts). Set this for production builds, e.g.:
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.your-domain.com
VITE_API_URL=/api

# Card payments need no key here: they go through Stripe's hosted Checkout, so
# the browser never touches Stripe's API directly. STRIPE_SECRET_KEY and
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET go in the backend's .env; without them checkout uses the
# deterministic stand-in provider and card orders complete without a real charge.

# Google Maps JavaScript API key, for the live driver map on the order page.
# Leave unset to run without a map: tracking degrades to a text panel showing
# the driver's distance and ETA. This key ships to the browser, so restrict it
# by HTTP referrer in the Google Cloud console and enable only the Maps
# JavaScript API on it. The Routes and Geocoding calls use the separate
# server-side GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY in the backend's .env.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
